Currently the code for experimenting with try, catch, exceptions and terminate function is located at lines:
    224 - 230
and commented.

With partial (complete) uncommenting it can be found that:
1) If only throw command is uncommented, then the custom terminate function will be executed and memory will be successsfully removed.
2) If the whole try-catch is unommented, then the terminate function will not be executed. ExploreBehavior object's constructor and destructor will be executed both.
3) If only ExploreBehavior object declaration and throw are left, then constructor will be executed but no destructor. The terminate function is also executed in this case. 